# Web Application Statistics Integration Walkthrough

The "Yakında" placeholder on the web app's `İstatistikler` tab has been entirely overhauled to mirror the exact comprehensive functionality of the iOS `StatisticsScreen.js`.

> [!SUCCESS]
> The Web Architecture is now actively fetching simulated profit constraints and pulling data globally directly from the `signals.db` repository, utilizing caching and interval pooling exactly like the smartphone interface.

## What Was Completed

- **Data Alignment**: Injected `loadStats` using `axios.get('/api/signals/stats')` natively inside `Dashboard.jsx`, creating a continuous 15-second data pull cycle from the EC2 AWS server.
- **Visual Symmetry**: The new desktop GUI integrates the aesthetic identifiers corresponding to the Native React framework (`#162336` wallet blue, glowing stats). It leverages flex boxes to dynamically restructure grids and handle window rescaling dynamically.
- **Component Availability**:
  - `Simulated Wallet Growth (PnL)`
  - `Wins (TP)` and `Losses (SL)` nodes with corresponding percentage tags
  - `Win Rate` and `Total Signals` elements
  - `Trades Reaching +2%` tracking panel representing solid movement analysis.

## Verification Check

You may instantly visualize the live components locally utilizing the active `npm run dev` pipeline running on your PC.

To view the live production deployment, Vercel has initiated the automated sync protocol directly from GitHub. The deployment will deploy the entire `Dashboard.jsx` component within the next 2 minutes. Navigate to the `/dashboard` route under `Stats` to verify the interface behavior natively on your smartphone browser.
